# `from` on the right of `union`: removed by a certain fix (DS0152).
mode: syntax
---- query
from a | union from 'b.csv'
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..28
  PIPELINE@0..27
    IDENT@0..4 "from"
    WHITESPACE@4..5 " "
    NAME_REF@5..6
      IDENT@5..6 "a"
    WHITESPACE@6..7 " "
    PIPE@7..8 "|"
    WHITESPACE@8..9 " "
    UNION_OP@9..27
      IDENT@9..14 "union"
      WHITESPACE@14..15 " "
      ERROR@15..19
        IDENT@15..19 "from"
      WHITESPACE@19..20 " "
      LITERAL@20..27
        STRING@20..27 "'b.csv'"
  WHITESPACE@27..28 "\n"

error[DS0152]: `from` is not written after `union`
  --> query:1:16
  |
1 | from a | union from 'b.csv'
  |                ^^^^ `union` takes a table directly
  |
  = help: remove `from`: `union 'b.csv'`
  = note: a pipeline on the right goes in parentheses: `(from t | where x > 1)`

with the machine-applicable fixes applied:
    from a | union 'b.csv'
which parses without errors
